  "text": "We are given:\n\n$$\na = \\frac{b + c}{x + 1}, \\quad b = \\frac{a + c}{y + 1}, \\quad c = \\frac{a + b}{z + 1},\n$$\n\nand the condition:\n\n$$\nxy + xz + yz = xyz.\n$$\n\nWe are also told that $x, y, z$ are the roots of the polynomial:\n\n$$\nt^3 + At^2 + Bt + C = 0.\n$$\n\nWe are to find the value of $\\frac{A + B}{C}$.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the Polynomial\n\nLet the polynomial be:\n\n$$\nt^3 + At^2 + Bt + C = 0.\n$$\n\nLet $x, y, z$ be its roots. Then:\n\n- $x + y + z = -A$,\n- $xy + xz + yz = B$,\n- $xyz = -C$.\n\nWe are given:\n\n$$\nxy + xz + yz = xyz.\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\nB = -C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $\\frac{A + B}{C}$ is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{A + B}{C} = \\frac{A - C}{C} = \\frac{A}{C} - 1.\n$$\n\nBut we don't know $A$ and $C$ directly. However, we can find $A$ and $C$ using the fact that:\n\n- $x + y + z = -A$,\n- $xy + xz + yz = B = -C$,\n- $xyz = -C$.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Use the Given Symmetry\n\nWe are told:\n\n$$\na = \\frac{b + c}{x + 1}, \\quad b = \\frac{a + c}{y + 1}, \\quad c = \\frac{a + b}{z + 1}.\n$$\n\nThis suggests a symmetric relationship among $a, b, c$. Let’s assume:\n\n$$\na = b = c.\n$$\n\nThen:\n\n$$\na = \\frac{a + a}{x + 1} \\Rightarrow a = \\frac{2a}{x + 1} \\Rightarrow x + 1 = 2 \\Rightarrow x = 1.\n$$\n\nSo, $x = 1$. Then:\n\n$$\nb = \\frac{a + a}{1 + 1} = \\frac{2a}{2} = a, \\quad \\text{so } b = a.\n$$\n\nThen:\n\n$$\nc = \\frac{a + a}{z + 1} = \\frac{2a}{z + 1} \\Rightarrow z + 1 = \\frac{2a}{c} \\Rightarrow z = \\frac{2a}{c} - 1.\n$$\n\nBut since $a = b = c$, we have:\n\n$$\nc = a = \\frac{2a}{z + 1} \\Rightarrow z + 1 = \\frac{2a}{a} = 2 \\Rightarrow z = 1.\n$$\n\nSo $x = y = z = 1$.\n\nTherefore, all the values are equal to 1.\n\nNow, plug into the polynomial:\n\n$$\nt^3 + At^2 + Bt + C = 0.\n$$\n\nSince $x = y = z = 1$, the polynomial becomes:\n\n$$\n(t - 1)^3 = 0.\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n- $x + y + z = 3 = -A \\Rightarrow A = -3$,\n- $xy + xz + yz = 3 = B = -C \\Rightarrow B = -C$,\n- $xyz = 1 = -C \\Rightarrow C = -1$.\n\nThus:\n\n$$\n\\frac{A + B}{C} = \\frac{-3 + (-1)}{-1} = \\frac{-4}{-1} = \\boxed{4}.\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{4}\n$$",
